cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MINUT, please cite both the software (this file) and the article (preferred-citation)."
type: software
title: "MINUT: Max-INtensity Untargeted Transformation for direct chemometric modeling of HRMS data"
abstract: >-
  MINUT bins each LC-HRMS run on a fixed (m/z, retention time) grid and keeps, in every bin, the most
  intense point together with its m/z and retention time, giving one feature vector per run without
  peak picking or alignment. The repository holds the transform, the deposited feature tables of the
  three case studies of the article (milk authenticity, lung cancer vs tuberculosis, COVID-19
  severity) and the notebooks that recompute every number, table and figure of the article.
